info.description:
EduPulse auth-service — Phase 4 of docs/API_V4.0_PARENT_ONBOARDING.md: teacher-initiated student + parent invite.
Only Phase 4 is implemented so far (invite a parent for a student already in the teacher's class). Phase 5 (parent account activation: OTP/profile/set-password) and Phase 6 (login) are not yet built — this collection stops at 'invite sent'.

Before running:
1. {{teacher_email}} / {{teacher_password}} must belong to an already-activated teacher account for {{branch_id}} (see postman_teacher_onboarding_collection.json to create one).
2. {{class_id}}, {{section_id}}, {{relationship_type_id}} must be filled in manually — these endpoints take raw ids, not names (only the bulk CSV/Excel upload accepts human-readable class/grade/relationship_type columns). Grab sample ids with:
   SELECT id, name FROM masters.classes;
   SELECT id, name FROM masters.sections;
   SELECT id, name FROM masters.relationship_type;
   against the tenant DB.
3. The raw parent invite token is never returned by the API — after 'Invite Single Parent' below, copy it from the auth-service console log line `[DEV] parent raw invite token: ...` if you need it for a future Phase 5 test.
